# Review: TerraPlugin

The spec is prose plus QA tests, so the only judged item is QA-1. The autocue flow
`autocue/planet.mjs` (tagged `@mdl ... test QA-1`) drives the create and reshape steps in a real
browser: it creates a planet, reseeds it, and nudges the water and tree-density sliders. It does not
assert that the same seed reproduces the same terrain, and it does not run the delete cleanup, so
QA-1 is partly automated. It is a recording driver, not part of CI.

Of 1 item: 0 done, 0 untested, 1 partial, 0 diverged, 0 missing.

